# SeatsBrokers — Cursor Rules
(Always loaded. Keep this short — it costs tokens every message.)

## Before doing anything
Read MEMORY.md first. It links to everything else. Do not scan the full
src/ tree unless you are actively editing a specific file — use
docs/COMPONENT_MAP.md and docs/PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md instead of re-reading
the codebase to answer "does X exist" or "where does Y live."

## Non-negotiables
- Brand name is SeatsBrokers (plural). Never "SeatsBroker."
- Primary color, fonts, and component conventions are defined in
  docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md — read that before making any style decision.
- New sections reuse the existing PageSections component vocabulary or the
  Live Console pattern (docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md) — don't invent new one-off
  section shapes without checking docs/COMPONENT_MAP.md first.

## Workflow
- One section/feature at a time unless told otherwise.
- After finishing any task, update docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md yourself.
- If you need context beyond MEMORY.md's links, ask which specific file to
  read rather than scanning the whole project.
